// Function 1
while n > 1 do
    for i = 1 to n do
        x = x + 1;
    end for
    n = floor(n / 2);
end while

// Function 2
for i = 1 to 100 * n do
    x = x + 1;
end for
\end{lstlisting}
Let $f_1(n)$ and $f_2(n)$ denote the number of times the statement ``$x = x + 1$'' is executed in Function 1 and Function 2, respectively.
